# Secrets. server/.env holds MSG91_AUTHKEY, the MSG91 widget token, JWT_SECRET and
# the Paytm merchant key. It must never be committed, and the rule belongs here
# rather than in a root file so it travels with the server package.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The live SQLite database and its WAL sidecars. The database holds real customer
# names, addresses, mobile numbers and order history, so it is excluded on the same
# grounds as the keys above - and unlike them it is large and never useful in a
# diff. hotel_darshan.db is what server/src/db.js opens by default.
hotel_darshan.db
hotel_darshan.db-shm
hotel_darshan.db-wal
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

node_modules
*.log
npm-debug.log*
